## Parent
- Spec: benchmark-gepa-overhaul
- Goals: G-4, G-5
- Depends on: bench-result-substrate, bench-panel-manifest, bench-model-judge, bench-prompt-files
- Frozen decisions: F-2, F-3, F-4, F-5, F-6

## Problem

Parent goal: Grow the benchmark with FeatureBench, the Gin render-context task, and a few cherry-picked tasks, in a format GEPA can optimize against once-run stored baselines, with a model judge for structural-tool applicability.

This curd is the loop that the other curds feed. The MCP instructions are compiled in (`src/mcp/mod.rs:76`) and byte-locked by a `#[cfg(test)]` test (`src/mcp/mod.rs:771-780`), so a text-only optimizer cannot change what agents see without a rebuild and a lock rewrite. Pinned variants can only be built from a remote git URL (`benchmark/variants.py:96-99`), so a local candidate commit cannot be served today. The stored row carries grader text in `correctness_reason` (`benchmark/run.py:849`): missing ground-truth strings (`benchmark/tasks/base.py:180`) and up to 1200 characters of held-out test output (`benchmark/tasks/gin_render_context_tasks.py:156-157,165`). A naive reflection step would therefore leak the grader into the model that rewrites tilth. Paired comparison exists (`benchmark/paired.py:141-160,195`), but it joins on task, model, and repetition, so frontier re-runs need frozen baseline rows at the same repetition numbers.

## Contract

The evolution loop (parent curd c5) adds `benchmark/evolve/` and two run.py seams. It changes no file under `src/**` or `prompts/**` itself; only candidate commits on a scratch branch do.

- **Candidate (F-2).** A candidate has five components: four text components, `prompts/mcp.md`, `prompts/tools/read.md`, `prompts/tools/search.md`, `prompts/tools/write.md`, and `src_patch`, a unified diff over `src/**`. The seed candidate holds those four files' bytes at `--seed-sha` and an empty `src_patch`. A materialized candidate is one commit on the scratch branch `evolve/<run-id>`, whose parent is its GEPA parent candidate's commit. Its identity in rows is the commit `git_sha` plus the `binary_sha256` of the binary built from it.
- **Engine (F-3).** `evolve.main` drives GEPA `optimize_anything` with the seed candidate, `evolve.evaluate` as the evaluator, the dev split as the dataset, and `--max-metric-calls` as the budget. GEPA's reflection model proposes the text components; the reflection model is a `claude -p` callable that runs through the shared auth guard and spend ledger. `src_patch` is proposed by `evolve.propose_src_patch`, registered as that component's custom proposer. GEPA's exact hook names are [speculating] until the pinned `gepa` release is read; `benchmark/evolve/engine.py` is the only module that imports `gepa`, so the tests stub it.
- **Reflective record (G-4, F-5).** For each paid-tier or cheap-tier dev rollout, `evolve.evaluate` builds one record from the stored JSONL row and its untruncated trajectory sidecar. The record holds every tool call's full input and output from the sidecar, the agent's final answer, and an allowlist of row fields: `task`, `prompt`, `mode`, `model`, `repetition`, `correct`, `pass_rate`, F2P/P2P pass and fail counts, `num_turns`, `total_cost_usd`, `duration_ms`, and `tool_calls`. It never holds `correctness_reason`, the task's `required_strings` or `forbidden_strings`, a gold patch, or held-out test source or output, and fields outside the allowlist never enter it. Agent-produced text stays verbatim even when it matches a ground-truth string, since a correct answer to `rg_trait_implementors` must name `Matcher`, `find_at`, and `RegexMatcher` (`benchmark/tasks/ripgrep_tasks.py:26`). GEPA side info, the reflection prompt, the proposer prompt, and the `judge.critique(row, trajectory)` input are built only from these records.
- **Excluded rollouts (F-5).** A rollout whose row has `contaminated: true` yields no record and no critique call. A row with no `contaminated` key stops the run with an error naming the row, rather than being scored. No test-split rollout ever yields a record, critique, side info entry, or proposer input; test-split cells run only inside `evolve.finish`.
- **Score (F-5).** A candidate's score is the mean grader `correct` over its paid-tier dev rollouts, with a contaminated rollout counted as incorrect. Per dev task, `evolve.evaluate` returns that task's mean `correct` over the candidate's rollouts as GEPA's per-instance score. Cheap-tier rollouts, test-split rollouts, applicability labels, and critiques never change it.
- **Judge gating (F-5).** Before any proposal, `evolve.main` obtains a cached `judge.applicability` label for every panel task and calls `judge.calibrate`, logging the agreement value. When the judge is calibrated, each record carries its task label and the rollout's critique, and the delta report adds per-label accuracy slices. When it is not, records carry neither, no critique call is made, and the run log and delta report say `labels: uncalibrated`. A judge answer outside c4's categorical label set yields no cached label.
- **Proposer isolation (F-2, F-5).** `evolve.propose_src_patch(worktree, records)` runs `claude -p` in a sparse worktree: a `git archive` export of `src/**`, `prompts/**`, `Cargo.toml`, and `Cargo.lock` at the parent commit, in a temp directory outside the tilth checkout, with no `.git`. The call passes `--tools Read,Edit,Write,Glob,Grep`, disallows `Bash`, `WebFetch`, `WebSearch`, `Agent`, and `Task`, loads no MCP server and no settings sources, and uses a per-call Claude config dir that copies auth only, as `_cell_claude_config` does (`benchmark/run.py:394`). The returned diff is the export's `src/**` changes; edits outside `src/**` are dropped and logged. The candidate is rejected, and nothing is committed, when any proposer tool call's input resolves to a path outside the export, or any tool input or output names `benchmark/`, the panel file path or basename, or the harness data directory. At HEAD no file under `src/` or `prompts/` contains the string `benchmark/`.
- **Applier (F-2, F-4).** `evolve.materialize(candidate)` works in a git worktree of the tilth repo at the parent commit and runs, in order:
  1. write the four text components;
  2. apply `src_patch`;
  3. reject the candidate when any changed path is outside `src/**` and `prompts/**`, or any changed line sits inside a `#[cfg(test)]` item, or in a file that is itself a `#[cfg(test)]` module such as `src/edit/integration_tests.rs` (declared at `src/edit/mod.rs:14-15`);
  4. regenerate `AGENTS.md` with `scripts/regen-agents-md.sh`;
  5. rewrite the byte-count, `starts_with`, and `ends_with` literals of `server_instructions_byte_lock` (`src/mcp/mod.rs:774,777-780`) to the new `prompts/mcp.md` byte length, its leading lines (as many as the current literal spans), and its last line;
  6. commit on `evolve/<run-id>` and return the sha.
  Every other `#[cfg(test)]` guard stays a guard that `just check` enforces: the remaining byte-lock assertions, `cwd_guidance_spans_present` (`src/mcp/mod.rs:2292`), the 2KB instruction checks (`src/mcp/mod.rs:1245-1250,2305`), `agents_md_matches_prompt_sources` (`src/mcp/mod.rs:1230`), the 13,779-byte surface cap (`src/mcp/mod.rs:816`), and `tool_descriptions_fit_2kb` (`src/mcp/tools/definitions.rs:522`).
- **Cascade (F-3, F-4).** `evolve.cascade(sha)` runs four stages and stops at the first failure with score 0 and the failing stage recorded in side info, with the tail of that stage's output:
  1. apply (materialize succeeded);
  2. `just check` in the candidate worktree;
  3. cheap tier: the panel's cheap tasks, one rollout each; it passes when the candidate's cheap-tier correctness is at least the seed's;
  4. paid tier: every dev task.
  Cells run through `run.run_plan` with `--candidate-sha`, which builds the tilth binary with `cargo build --release --locked` at that commit and records its `git_sha` and `binary_sha256` in the row's variant metadata (`benchmark/run.py:81-99`). The seed's cheap-tier and paid-tier rows come from the store when present.
- **Baselines (G-5).** The baseline arm is mode `baseline` (`benchmark/config.py:142-148`). The first evolve run over a panel buys each baseline cell once: every dev and cheap task at repetitions 1 to 1 + R, where R is the re-run count. Later runs, and every candidate in a run, answer those cells from the c1 store and write them to the run's output JSONL with `reused: true`. c1's drift refusal applies: a planned baseline cell with a completed row only under a different key refuses the run unless `--refreeze-baselines` is passed, which buys each drifted cell once under the new key. Test-split baseline cells are bought the same way, once, inside `evolve.finish`.
- **Frontier re-runs (F-3).** A candidate whose first-rollout per-task score vector is not dominated by any current frontier member is re-run R more times on every dev task at repetitions 2 to 1 + R. Those repetitions give fresh run keys, so the store never answers a re-run with the first rollout. Only the mean over all 1 + R rollouts reaches GEPA, so no candidate joins the frontier on one rollout. A dominated candidate is not re-run.
- **Delta report (G-5).** For every candidate that reaches the paid tier, `evolve` writes to the run log a delta report computed with `paired.paired_accuracy_delta` and `paired.paired_cpc_delta` over the candidate's tilth rows and the stored baseline rows at the same task, model, and repetition. It never invokes a baseline-arm runner to build it.
- **Stop and finish (F-4).** The search stops when `--max-metric-calls` is spent, when P consecutive paid-tier candidates leave the best frontier mean dev score unimproved, when the spend ceiling would be crossed, or on a quota stop. Then `evolve.finish(frontier)` scores the two best non-seed frontier candidates by dev mean, plus the seed, once on the test split at repetitions 1 to 1 + R. The winner is the finalist with the highest test-split mean correctness (contaminated counted incorrect), ties broken by dev mean and then by earlier commit. When the winner is not the seed, finish pushes `evolve/<run-id>` and opens exactly one draft PR whose head is the winner commit and whose body holds the dev and test delta reports. It never merges, never enables auto-merge, and refuses to open the PR when the seed-to-winner diff touches a path outside `src/**`, `prompts/**`, and `AGENTS.md`. When the seed wins, finish opens no PR and logs `no improvement`. A quota stop or ceiling stop skips finish and opens no PR.
- **Spend and auth (F-6).** `evolve.main` requires `--max-usd` and exits before any model call without it. One c1 spend ledger instance spans every paid call in the run: agent cells, judge calls, reflection calls, and proposer calls. Each call first passes the shared auth guard, which refuses it when `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is set, and the ledger check, which stops the run before a call whose estimate would cross the ceiling. A cell's estimate follows c1's tiers. A reflection, judge, or proposer call's estimate is the mean cost of earlier calls of the same kind in this run, else `--cell-estimate-usd`. A usage-limit rejection in any call stops the run with `infra:quota` in the run log, leaving stored rows reusable. The run log and delta reports carry no task-growth gate verdict.
- **Agent-decided defaults.**
  - [AGENT-DECIDED] R = 3 re-runs and plateau P = 5, flags `--reruns` and `--plateau`; this settles the parent open question. A plateau round counts only candidates that reach the paid tier, so a streak of build failures does not end the search. Alternative: count every proposed candidate.
  - [AGENT-DECIDED] One model per evolve run, `--model` defaulting to `haiku` because the repo guidance tests instruction changes on haiku. Alternative: `sonnet`, the `run.py` default.
  - [AGENT-DECIDED] Finalists are the two best non-seed frontier candidates plus the seed. Alternative: the three best, with the seed excluded.
  - [AGENT-DECIDED] The proposer worktree is a `git archive` export with no `.git`, a stricter form of the parent's sparse worktree, so no git metadata links back to the full checkout. Alternative: `git worktree add` with sparse checkout.
  - [AGENT-DECIDED] A row missing the `contaminated` key stops the run. Alternative: count it as contaminated and continue.
  - [AGENT-DECIDED] `--candidate-sha` builds from the local commit instead of going through an experiment manifest, because `benchmark/variants.py:96-99` admits only remote git URLs. Alternative: relax that check to accept `file://`.
  - [AGENT-DECIDED] Cheap-tier dev rollouts also yield reflective records under the same stripping rules, so reflection sees why a candidate failed the cheap tier. Alternative: paid-tier records only.

## Grounding

| Probe | Outcome | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| wiki | hit | `.hallouminate/wiki/mcp-instructions-limits-and-format.md`: `prompts/mcp.md` is one byte-locked file of at most 2,048 chars and tool descriptions are truncated at 2,048 chars each, so the cascade `just check` stage is the size guard; `.hallouminate/wiki/benchmark-harness-gotchas.md`: a stale installed binary served old instructions for weeks, so candidate cells must build from the candidate commit and record `binary_sha256` |
| explorer | hit | HEAD `4cafeea` read with `git show`: `SERVER_INSTRUCTIONS` via `include_str!` at `src/mcp/mod.rs:76`, byte lock at `src/mcp/mod.rs:771-780` (1966 bytes, `starts_with` two lines, `ends_with` last line), `prompts/tools/read.md` already loaded by `include_str!` at `src/mcp/tools/definitions.rs:4` while the `tilth_search` and `tilth_write` descriptions are inline at `definitions.rs:10,117`; `scripts/regen-agents-md.sh` writes a header plus `prompts/mcp.md`; `paired.py` pairs on task, model, repetition (`paired.py:141-160`); variants require remote URLs (`variants.py:96-99`); `correctness_reason` at `run.py:849`; file-level test module at `src/edit/mod.rs:14-15` |

## Approach

1. **Engine skeleton and seed (F-3, F-2).** Add `benchmark/evolve/` with `engine.py` as the only `gepa` importer and pin `gepa` in `benchmark/requirements.txt`. `evolve.main` loads the panel with `panels.load_panel`, reads the seed's four text components at `--seed-sha`, refuses when any is missing, and passes the seed candidate, `evolve.evaluate`, and `--max-metric-calls` to `optimize_anything`.
2. **Spend and auth first (F-6).** `evolve.main` builds one c1 spend ledger from `--max-usd` and routes every cell, judge, reflection, and proposer call through the shared auth guard and that ledger. A quota rejection anywhere stops the run.
3. **Records and judge gating (F-5, G-4).** Build reflective records from stored rows and sidecars with the field allowlist. Drop contaminated and test-split rollouts. Run the judge preflight, and attach labels and critiques only when calibrated.
4. **Proposer and applier (F-2, F-4, F-5).** `propose_src_patch` runs the isolated proposer and scans its trajectory. `materialize` applies, enforces the allowlist and the `#[cfg(test)]` guard, regenerates `AGENTS.md`, rewrites the byte-lock literals, and commits.
5. **Cascade, baselines, and frontier (F-3, F-4, G-5).** Add `run.run_plan` and `--candidate-sha`. `cascade` runs apply, `just check`, the cheap tier, and the paid tier, buying baselines once and reusing them. Re-run frontier-eligible candidates R times on fresh repetitions and write a paired delta report per paid-tier candidate.
6. **Finish (F-4, F-2).** Score finalists once on the test split, pick the winner, and open one draft PR through a PR client seam (`gh pr create --draft`) only for a non-seed winner.

## Interface sketches

```text
slice:            NEW SLICE benchmark/evolve/ + benchmark (existing harness)
spine step:       entry (evolve.main) + workflow (cascade, finish) + infra (materialize, proposer worktree)
public interface: evolve.main(--panel PATH, --max-usd FLOAT, --max-metric-calls INT, --seed-sha SHA, --model NAME, --reruns INT, --plateau INT, --cell-estimate-usd FLOAT, --refreeze-baselines)  (F-3, F-6)
public interface: evolve.evaluate(candidate, task) -> (score, side_info)  (F-3, F-5)
public interface: evolve.propose_src_patch(worktree, records) -> diff  (F-2, F-5)
public interface: evolve.materialize(candidate) -> sha  (F-2, F-4)
public interface: evolve.cascade(sha) -> (score, side_info)  (F-3, F-4)
public interface: evolve.finish(frontier) -> PullRequest | None  (F-4)
public interface: run.run_plan(cells, *, ledger, candidate_sha, refreeze_baselines) -> list[Row]; run.py --candidate-sha SHA  (F-2, F-6)
consumed:         baselines.lookup / baselines.store, c1 spend ledger and auth guard (c1); panels.load_panel(path) -> Panel(cheap, dev, test) (c3); judge.applicability(task) -> Label, judge.critique(row, trajectory) -> str, judge.calibrate(labels) -> Agreement (c4); paired.paired_accuracy_delta, paired.paired_cpc_delta
private:          GEPA adapter (engine.py), reflective record builder and field allowlist, proposer trajectory scan, cfg(test) span detector, byte-lock literal rewriter, frontier dominance check, plateau counter, finalist selection, PR client
crust delta:      new package benchmark/evolve/; new run.py function run_plan and flag --candidate-sha; gepa pinned in benchmark/requirements.txt; evolve run log under benchmark/results/evolve/<run-id>/
arrows:           evolve -> run, baselines, panels, judge, paired; engine -> gepa; no arrow from tilth src/ into benchmark/
```

## Acceptance
- AC-1: WHEN evolve builds a reflective record for a cheap-tier or paid-tier dev rollout THE SYSTEM SHALL build it from the stored JSONL row and its untruncated trajectory sidecar, holding every tool call's full input and output and the agent's final answer verbatim even when they contain a ground-truth string, keep from grading only `correct`, `pass_rate`, and F2P/P2P counts, admit no row field outside the record allowlist, exclude `correctness_reason`, `required_strings`, `forbidden_strings`, gold patches, and held-out test source and output, and use only that record as GEPA side info and as the `judge.critique` input.  (G-4, F-5)
- AC-2: WHEN a rollout is contaminated THE SYSTEM SHALL build no reflective record and make no critique call for it, WHEN a rollout belongs to the test split THE SYSTEM SHALL never put it in a record, critique, side info entry, or proposer input, and WHEN a dev rollout is neither THE SYSTEM SHALL build exactly one record for it.  (F-5, G-4)
- AC-3: WHEN the cascade scores a candidate that reaches the paid tier THE SYSTEM SHALL return the mean grader `correct` over its paid-tier dev rollouts as the only score, counting a contaminated rollout as incorrect, unchanged by any applicability label, critique, cheap-tier row, or test-split row, and WHEN a scored row lacks the `contaminated` key THE SYSTEM SHALL stop the run with an error naming that row.  (F-5, F-3)
- AC-4: WHEN an evolve run starts THE SYSTEM SHALL hold a cached categorical applicability label for every panel task and log the judge agreement value before any proposal; WHEN the judge is calibrated THE SYSTEM SHALL attach each task label and rollout critique to its reflective record and slice the delta report by label; WHEN it is uncalibrated THE SYSTEM SHALL attach neither, make no critique call, and mark the run log and delta report uncalibrated.  (F-5)
- AC-5: WHEN evolve proposes a `src_patch` THE SYSTEM SHALL run the proposer in an export holding only `src/**`, `prompts/**`, `Cargo.toml`, and `Cargo.lock` with no `.git`, with Bash, web tools, and MCP servers disabled, return the export's `src/**` changes as the diff, and reject the candidate without a commit when any proposer tool input resolves outside the export or any tool input or output names `benchmark/`, the panel file, or the harness data directory.  (F-2, F-5)
- AC-6: WHEN evolve materializes a candidate THE SYSTEM SHALL write the text components, apply the patch, reject any change outside `src/**` and `prompts/**` or inside a `#[cfg(test)]` item or `#[cfg(test)]` module file, regenerate `AGENTS.md`, rewrite the byte-count, `starts_with`, and `ends_with` literals of `server_instructions_byte_lock` to match the new `prompts/mcp.md`, and only then commit on the scratch branch with the parent candidate's commit as parent.  (F-2, F-4)
- AC-7: WHEN a candidate commit exists THE SYSTEM SHALL evaluate it through apply, `just check`, the cheap tier (passing when its cheap-tier correctness is at least the seed's), then the paid tier, SHALL stop at the first failing stage with score 0 and that stage recorded, and SHALL serve candidate cells from a binary built at that commit with its `git_sha` and `binary_sha256` in the row.  (F-3, F-4)
- AC-8: WHEN the first evolve run over a panel starts on an empty store THE SYSTEM SHALL make exactly one baseline-arm runner call per baseline cell, WHEN a later run over an unchanged panel, agent CLI, and env fingerprint runs THE SYSTEM SHALL make no baseline-arm runner call and write those rows to its output JSONL with `reused: true`, and WHEN a baseline cell drifted to a different key THE SYSTEM SHALL refuse to start unless `--refreeze-baselines` is passed, after which it buys that cell once under the new key.  (G-5, F-3)
- AC-9: WHEN a candidate's first-rollout per-task scores are not dominated by the frontier THE SYSTEM SHALL re-run it R times on every dev task at fresh repetitions before its scores reach GEPA, WHEN they are dominated THE SYSTEM SHALL not re-run it, WHEN a candidate reaches the paid tier THE SYSTEM SHALL write a paired delta report of accuracy and cost per correct against stored baseline rows without a baseline-arm runner call, and WHEN P consecutive paid-tier candidates leave the best dev mean unimproved THE SYSTEM SHALL stop proposing.  (F-3, G-5)
- AC-10: WHEN the search stops normally THE SYSTEM SHALL score the two best non-seed frontier candidates and the seed once on the test split, and WHEN the winner is not the seed THE SYSTEM SHALL open exactly one draft PR whose head commit passed `just check`, whose seed-to-winner diff touches only `src/**`, `prompts/**`, and `AGENTS.md`, and whose body holds the delta reports, and SHALL never merge it; WHEN the seed wins THE SYSTEM SHALL open no PR.  (F-4, F-2)
- AC-11: WHEN an evolve run starts without `--max-usd` THE SYSTEM SHALL exit before any model call; WHEN any agent cell, judge call, reflection call, or proposer call starts THE SYSTEM SHALL refuse it with `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` set, count its cost against the one run-wide ceiling, and stop before a call whose estimate would cross it; WHEN any call reports a usage-limit rejection or the next call would cross the ceiling THE SYSTEM SHALL stop the run without running finish or opening a PR; and the run log SHALL carry no task-growth gate verdict.  (F-6)
- AC-12: WHEN an evolve run starts THE SYSTEM SHALL refuse before any model call if any of `prompts/mcp.md`, `prompts/tools/read.md`, `prompts/tools/search.md`, or `prompts/tools/write.md` is missing at `--seed-sha`, and otherwise SHALL call GEPA `optimize_anything` with a seed candidate holding those four files' bytes and an empty `src_patch`, `evolve.evaluate` as evaluator, the dev split as dataset, and `--max-metric-calls` as budget.  (F-3, F-2)

